From: Trinity AI Agent <267220563+trinity-ai-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:23:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] TCFraming: carry a requested-outputs mask in the v2
 frame header

Byte 5 of a v2 frame header was a flags byte that had to be 0. It is
now the requested-outputs mask: bit n is set for ECodecType n.

- reflector -> tcd: the codec fields the reflector wants in the reply.
  0 means every codec, as before.
- tcd -> reflector: the codec fields that hold data.

The receive queue now carries the mask with each packet (STCRequest).
This change only moves the mask through the link. The next change uses
it in the Controller. v2 framing has not been released, so the header
can change without a version bump. Raw framing does not change.
